content.text:
No COPILOT_GITHUB_TOKEN, I'm using BYOK. But for it to work I need that workflow on my tailnet to reach my gateway. The openwiki workflow does this and has the pattern. Also have to set some config settings; need a providers.json with:

<pasted_content id="c9d5">
{
  "providers": [
    {
      "name": "lab-proxy",
      "type": "anthropic",
      "baseUrl": "https://anthropic-oauth-proxy.tailfb3ea.ts.net",
      "apiKey": "-"
    }
  ],
  "models": [
    {
      "id": "claude-opus-5-5",
      "provider": "lab-proxy",
      "maxContextWindowTokens": 1000000,
      "maxPromptTokens": 872000,
      "maxOutputTokens": 128000
    }
  ]
}
</pasted_content id="c9d5">

Also need models[].capabilities.supports.vision set to true, 
models[].capabilities.supports.adaptive_thinking set to required,
models[].capabilities.supports.reasoning_effort set to ["low", "medium", "high"]

By default, this file is located at ~/.copilot/providers.json. Override its location with the COPILOT_PROVIDERS_CONFIG environment variable. That file does not exist on my host so add it to the repo instead. You can add all this just don't commit yet. I have a few more things after this

